# Centuries Mutual Labs Mandate

This repository is the Centuries Mutual Labs research, quantitative analysis, AI, and market intelligence laboratory. It is NOT a website, insurance CRM, or production application. Production apps live in GitLab.

## Build

- Market/economic regime detection, forecasting, healthcare/insurance intelligence
- Feature engineering, statistical/risk modeling, signals, backtesting, ML/RL/NLP
- Structured APIs and event bus for downstream consumers

## Architecture

- Keep modules independent (`ingestion`, `features`, `models`, `backtests`, `strategies`, `api`, `sdk`, `events`)
- Prefer dependency injection and composition; avoid tight coupling
- Models implement shared protocols (`RegimeModel`, `SignalModel`, `ForecastModel`, etc.)
- All engineered features live in the single feature store—never duplicate calculations
- Predictive models must be backtested (Sharpe, Sortino, drawdown, classification metrics, OOS, walk-forward)
- Notebooks are experimental only; promote validated work into modules
- APIs return structured JSON; never couple APIs to UI

## Forbidden in this repo

Do not build: authentication, user management, insurance CRM, marketing pages, website layouts, frontend dashboards, customer portals, or business CRUD.

## Engineering

Prefer readability, correctness, determinism, reproducibility, modularity, testability. No secrets in git—use environment variables. Version models independently (data, params, metrics, features).
